---
import FutureTechMissionFrame from '../../../../components/FutureTechMissionFrame.astro';
---
<FutureTechMissionFrame
  missionNumber="8"
  title="Creator Certification"
  tagline="You built it. You improved it. Now prove you understand it."
  question="Can you prove that you are ready to complete Creator Foundations?"
  success="I can test, improve and explain my Creator Challenge independently, and I can show that I understand the Level 1 skills I used to create it."
  try4Text="Check → Trace → Change One Thing → Test Again"
  stages={['Retrieve It','Inspect It','Improve It','Prove It','Prepare to Certify','Certify']}
  statusLabel="FINAL MISSION"
>
  <section class="final-brief" aria-label="Mission 8 reminder">
    <span>THIS IS NOT ANOTHER PROJECT</span>
    <p>Bring back your <b>Mission 7 Creator Challenge</b>. Make <b>one smart improvement</b>, prove that your creation works, and show that you understand the decisions behind it.</p>
    <strong>Small project + strong understanding beats a huge project you cannot explain.</strong>
  </section>

  <div class="cert-flow" aria-label="Mission 8 certification process">
    <span>RETRIEVE</span><b>→</b><span>INSPECT</span><b>→</b><span>IMPROVE</span><b>→</b><span>PROVE</span><b>→</b><span>PREPARE</span><b>→</b><span>CERTIFY</span>
  </div>
  <p class="flow-note"><b>Use your Mission 7 creation.</b> Work through the six stages in order. Do not start over unless Mr. John tells you to.</p>

  <section id="stage-1" class="stage">
    <div class="stage-head"><span class="stage-number">01</span><div><p class="stage-kicker">BRING BACK YOUR CREATION</p><h2 class="stage-title">Retrieve It</h2></div></div>
    <p class="intro">Open the <b>same Creator Challenge you used in Mission 7</b>. Your first job is simple: make sure you have the correct version and that the important part still works.</p>

    <div class="same-path">
      <strong>STAY ON YOUR MISSION 7 PATH</strong>
      <p>Use the same path you completed in Mission 7. You are not choosing again.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="path-id-grid">
      <article class="path-card coding"><span>PATH A</span><strong>CODING</strong><small>SOFTWARE CREATOR</small><p>Bring back your Mission 7 program, game or digital experience.</p></article>
      <article class="path-card robotics"><span>PATH B</span><strong>ROBOTICS</strong><small>SYSTEMS BUILDER</small><p>Bring back your Mission 7 code and robotic system.</p></article>
      <article class="path-card design"><span>PATH C</span><strong>3D DESIGN</strong><small>PRODUCT DESIGNER</small><p>Bring back your Mission 7 Tinkercad model.</p></article>
    </div>

    <div class="tool-grid">
      <article><strong>CODING</strong><a class="tool-launch external" href="https://makecode.microbit.org/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Open MakeCode for micro:bit ↗</a><a class="tool-launch secondary external" href="https://arcade.makecode.com/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Open MakeCode Arcade ↗</a><small>Open the platform you used for Mission 7.</small></article>
      <article><strong>ROBOTICS</strong><a class="tool-launch external" href="https://makecode.microbit.org/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Open MakeCode for micro:bit ↗</a><small>Collect your Hummingbird station only when you are ready to work with it.</small></article>
      <article><strong>3D DESIGN</strong><a class="tool-launch external" href="https://www.tinkercad.com/3d-design/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Open Tinkercad 3D Design ↗</a><small>Open your Mission 7 model. A physical print is not required.</small></article>
    </div>

    <p class="path-instruction"><b>Open only your path.</b> The other routes are here for other creators.</p>
    <div class="path-details">
      <details class="path-detail coding">
        <summary><span>PATH A</span><strong>CODING — RETRIEVE CHECK</strong></summary>
        <div class="check-list"><span>☐ I opened the correct Mission 7 project.</span><span>☐ The main interaction still works.</span><span>☐ I can identify the main interaction I will demonstrate.</span></div>
      </details>
      <details class="path-detail robotics">
        <summary><span>PATH B</span><strong>ROBOTICS — RETRIEVE CHECK</strong></summary>
        <div class="check-list"><span>☐ I opened the correct Mission 7 code.</span><span>☐ I have the correct Hummingbird equipment.</span><span>☐ I checked connections before powering on.</span><span>☐ The core system still works.</span></div>
      </details>
      <details class="path-detail design">
        <summary><span>PATH C</span><strong>3D DESIGN — RETRIEVE CHECK</strong></summary>
        <div class="check-list"><span>☐ I opened the correct Mission 7 design.</span><span>☐ I found the final version.</span><span>☐ The important dimensions and features are still there.</span></div>
      </details>
    </div>

    <p class="success"><b>Core project working?</b> Continue to Inspect It.</p>
    <p class="warning"><b>Something broken?</b> Repair the Mission 7 creation before trying to improve it.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="stage-2" class="stage">
    <div class="stage-head"><span class="stage-number">02</span><div><p class="stage-kicker">LOOK AT IT LIKE A CREATOR</p><h2 class="stage-title">Inspect It</h2></div></div>
    <p class="intro">Your creation already works. Now look at it again and ask: <b>If I had ten more minutes to make one part better, what would I change?</b></p>

    <div class="inspect-route">
      <article><span>WORKS</span><strong>What already works well?</strong><p>A short thought is enough.</p></article>
      <article><span>NOTICE</span><strong>What could work better?</strong><p>Look at how it works, feels, fits, responds or communicates.</p></article>
      <article><span>CHOOSE</span><strong>Pick ONE improvement that matters.</strong><p>You are improving your project—not rebuilding it.</p></article>
    </div>

    <div class="good-improvement">
      <strong>A GOOD MISSION 8 IMPROVEMENT IS...</strong>
      <span><b>USEFUL</b>It makes something work better.</span>
      <span><b>TESTABLE</b>You can check whether the change helped.</span>
      <span><b>SMALL</b>You can finish it during Mission 8.</span>
    </div>
    <p class="warning">If your idea needs an entirely different creation, several new features or unfamiliar technology, <b>choose something smaller.</b></p>

    <p class="path-instruction"><b>Open only your path.</b> These are ideas, not required upgrades.</p>
    <div class="path-details">
      <details class="path-detail coding"><summary><span>PATH A</span><strong>CODING — POSSIBLE IMPROVEMENTS</strong></summary><div class="chips"><span>adjust difficulty</span><span>fix unreliable scoring</span><span>improve feedback</span><span>adjust timing</span><span>clarify instructions</span><span>simplify unnecessary code</span><span>fix a condition</span></div><p><b>Ask:</b> What would make the program work better for the user?</p></details>
      <details class="path-detail robotics"><summary><span>PATH B</span><strong>ROBOTICS — POSSIBLE IMPROVEMENTS</strong></summary><div class="chips"><span>improve a threshold</span><span>improve consistency</span><span>adjust servo position</span><span>make an output clearer</span><span>secure a component</span><span>simplify unreliable behaviour</span><span>improve mounting</span></div><p><b>Ask:</b> What would make the system more reliable or useful?</p></details>
      <details class="path-detail design"><summary><span>PATH C</span><strong>3D DESIGN — POSSIBLE IMPROVEMENTS</strong></summary><div class="chips"><span>improve stability</span><span>adjust fit</span><span>correct a dimension</span><span>strengthen a weak section</span><span>improve a hole or slot</span><span>reduce unnecessary material</span><span>improve alignment</span></div><p><b>Ask:</b> What would make the object work better as a real product?</p></details>
    </div>

    <div class="evidence-one"><strong>I NOTICED...</strong><p>What could work better?</p><small><b>One sentence is enough.</b></small></div>
  </section>

  <section id="stage-3" class="stage">
    <div class="stage-head"><span class="stage-number">03</span><div><p class="stage-kicker">ONE CHANGE FOR A REASON</p><h2 class="stage-title">Improve It</h2></div></div>
    <p class="intro">Make the improvement you chose. <b>Do not add extra features while you are here.</b> Your goal is to make one part of your existing creation noticeably better.</p>

    <div class="improve-route"><span><b>NOTICE</b>I know what I want to improve.</span><span><b>CHANGE</b>I make one focused change.</span><span><b>TEST</b>I check whether it helped.</span><span><b>DECIDE</b>I keep it, adjust it or undo it.</span></div>

    <div class="try4"><strong>STUCK? TRY 4</strong>
      <div class="try-grid">
        <article><b>1 — CHECK</b><p>What exactly is not working?</p></article>
        <article><b>2 — TRACE</b><p><strong>Coding:</strong> Input → Code → Decision → Result<br/><strong>Robotics:</strong> Input/Sensor → Port → Code → Output<br/><strong>3D:</strong> Shape → Size → Position → Group/Cut → Purpose</p></article>
        <article><b>3 — CHANGE ONE THING</b><p>Change one possible cause.</p></article>
        <article><b>4 — TEST AGAIN</b><p>Did the change help?</p></article>
      </div>
      <p>Still stuck? Ask another creator what they notice. Then ask Mr. John.</p>
    </div>

    <p class="warning"><b>ROBOTICS SAFETY:</b> Unsure about power, wiring or possible equipment damage? Stop and ask immediately. Safety problems do not require TRY 4 first.</p>

    <div class="evidence-grid">
      <article><strong>I NOTICED...</strong><p>What could work better?</p></article>
      <article><strong>I CHANGED...</strong><p>What did you change?</p></article>
      <article><strong>I TESTED...</strong><p>How did you check it?</p></article>
      <article><strong>AFTER THE CHANGE...</strong><p>Did it work better?</p></article>
    </div>
    <p class="mini-note"><b>Keep each answer short.</b> You are recording evidence, not writing a report.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="stage-4" class="stage">
    <div class="stage-head"><span class="stage-number">04</span><div><p class="stage-kicker">RUN ONE CLEAN FINAL TEST</p><h2 class="stage-title">Prove It</h2></div></div>
    <p class="intro">Now prove the <b>core creation works</b>. Choose the test that gives the clearest evidence. You do not need to demonstrate every feature.</p>

    <p class="path-instruction"><b>Open only your path.</b> Run the final proof that fits your creation.</p>
    <div class="path-details">
      <details class="path-detail coding">
        <summary><span>PATH A</span><strong>CODING / SOFTWARE CREATOR</strong></summary>
        <p>Run your creation from a normal starting point.</p>
        <div class="route"><span>INPUT</span><span>PROGRAM RESPONSE</span><span>MEANINGFUL RESULT</span></div>
        <div class="check-list"><span>☐ The user can start or control the important action.</span><span>☐ The important code behaves as expected.</span><span>☐ The project reaches its intended result.</span><span>☐ I can repeat the test.</span></div>
      </details>
      <details class="path-detail robotics">
        <summary><span>PATH B</span><strong>ROBOTICS / SYSTEMS BUILDER</strong></summary>
        <p>Start your system safely and demonstrate the important behaviour.</p>
        <div class="route"><span>INPUT / SENSOR</span><span>DECISION</span><span>PHYSICAL OUTPUT</span></div>
        <div class="check-list"><span>☐ Hardware is connected correctly.</span><span>☐ The system starts safely.</span><span>☐ The important input or sensor works.</span><span>☐ The expected physical response happens.</span><span>☐ I can repeat the test.</span></div>
      </details>
      <details class="path-detail design">
        <summary><span>PATH C</span><strong>3D DESIGN / PRODUCT DESIGNER</strong></summary>
        <p>Inspect the final digital model from more than one view.</p>
        <div class="route"><span>PURPOSE</span><span>DIMENSIONS</span><span>IMPORTANT FEATURES</span><span>PRINTABILITY</span></div>
        <div class="check-list"><span>☐ Important dimensions are intentional.</span><span>☐ Major shapes are positioned correctly.</span><span>☐ Grouped/cut features work as intended.</span><span>☐ The model supports its intended purpose.</span><span>☐ The design appears reasonably manufacturable.</span></div>
        <p class="success"><b>A physical print is NOT required for certification.</b></p>
      </details>
    </div>

    <div class="proof-card"><strong>CAN YOU PROVE IT?</strong><span><b>What did you test?</b></span><span><b>What happened?</b></span><span><b>How do you know it worked?</b></span><small>No written response is required unless Mr. John asks for one.</small></div>

    <div class="stop-card"><strong>STOP ADDING FEATURES</strong><p>If your creation works and your final test is complete, <b>do not keep changing it just because you have time.</b></p><small>Your next job is to prepare to explain what you already made.</small></div>
  </section>

  <section id="stage-5" class="stage">
    <div class="stage-head"><span class="stage-number">05</span><div><p class="stage-kicker">MAKE SURE YOU ARE READY</p><h2 class="stage-title">Prepare to Certify</h2></div></div>
    <p class="intro">Certification is a short conversation with Mr. John. You do <b>not</b> need a speech. You do need to understand your own work.</p>

    <div class="ready-card">
      <strong>CERTIFICATION READY?</strong>
      <div class="check-list"><span>☐ My creation works well enough to demonstrate.</span><span>☐ I made one Mission 8 improvement.</span><span>☐ I tested the improvement.</span><span>☐ I completed one final proof test.</span><span>☐ I can explain what my creation is supposed to do.</span><span>☐ I can explain one important technical decision.</span><span>☐ I can explain what I improved and why.</span><span>☐ My file is saved.</span><span>☐ My equipment/workspace is organized.</span></div>
      <span class="ready-action">ALL CHECKED? ADD YOUR NAME TO THE CLASS READY-FOR-CHECK SYSTEM.</span>
    </div>

    <div class="check-preview">
      <strong>YOUR CHECK HAS FOUR PARTS</strong>
      <article><b>1 — SHOW IT</b><p>Demonstrate your creation.</p></article>
      <article><b>2 — EXPLAIN IT</b><p>Answer one technical question about your pathway.</p></article>
      <article><b>3 — IMPROVE IT</b><p>Explain your Mission 8 improvement.</p></article>
      <article><b>4 — PREDICT IT</b><p>Explain what you think would happen if one technical detail changed.</p></article>
    </div>
    <p class="concept">You do not know the exact questions ahead of time. That is okay. <b>If you understand your own project, you are ready.</b></p>

    <p class="path-instruction"><b>Open only your path.</b> You might be asked about one of these areas—not all of them.</p>
    <div class="path-details">
      <details class="path-detail coding"><summary><span>PATH A</span><strong>CODING — BE READY TO TALK ABOUT</strong></summary><div class="chips"><span>inputs</span><span>variables</span><span>decisions</span><span>repeating behaviour</span><span>user interaction</span><span>testing</span><span>debugging</span><span>your final improvement</span></div></details>
      <details class="path-detail robotics"><summary><span>PATH B</span><strong>ROBOTICS — BE READY TO TALK ABOUT</strong></summary><div class="chips"><span>input or sensor</span><span>Hummingbird ports</span><span>code decision</span><span>physical output</span><span>threshold</span><span>Sense → Think → Act</span><span>troubleshooting</span><span>your final improvement</span></div></details>
      <details class="path-detail design"><summary><span>PATH C</span><strong>3D DESIGN — BE READY TO TALK ABOUT</strong></summary><div class="chips"><span>dimensions</span><span>grouped shapes</span><span>holes/cuts/recesses</span><span>alignment</span><span>purpose</span><span>printability</span><span>revision</span><span>your final improvement</span></div></details>
    </div>

    <div class="waiting-card"><strong>WAITING FOR YOUR CHECK?</strong><div><span>Run your final test again.</span><span>Remove unnecessary code.</span><span>Clean up your digital workspace.</span><span>Inspect your CAD model.</span><span>Organize hardware.</span><span>Help another creator test.</span><span>Prepare your project for the optional showcase.</span></div><small><b>Do not start a major change while you wait.</b></small></div>
  </section>

  <section id="stage-6" class="stage checkpoint">
    <div class="stage-head"><span class="stage-number">06</span><div><p class="stage-kicker">SHOW WHAT YOU CAN DO</p><h2 class="stage-title">Creator Certification Check</h2></div></div>
    <p class="intro">This is not a presentation and it is not a written exam. It is a short individual check to prove that <b>you understand the work you created.</b></p>
    <p class="success"><b>Expected time: about 3–4 minutes.</b></p>

    <div class="cert-steps">
      <article><span>1</span><strong>SHOW IT</strong><p>Mr. John: <b>“Show me what you made.”</b></p><small>Start with the important part. You do not need to explain every feature.</small></article>
      <article><span>2</span><strong>EXPLAIN IT</strong><p>Answer one technical question about your project.</p><small>The question will match your pathway and your own creation.</small></article>
      <article><span>3</span><strong>TELL WHAT YOU IMPROVED</strong><p>Mr. John: <b>“What did you improve for Mission 8?”</b></p><small>Explain what you noticed, changed, tested and learned from the result.</small></article>
      <article><span>4</span><strong>PREDICT ONE CHANGE</strong><p>Explain what you think would happen if one technical detail changed.</p><small>You usually do not have to make the change. Explain your prediction and why.</small></article>
    </div>

    <p class="path-instruction"><b>Question examples only.</b> These show the kind of thinking you may be asked to do.</p>
    <div class="path-details">
      <details class="path-detail coding"><summary><span>PATH A</span><strong>CODING — QUESTION TYPES</strong></summary><div class="question-grid"><span>What controls this action?</span><span>What is this value doing?</span><span>Where does the program make a choice?</span><span>If this value became larger, what might happen?</span></div></details>
      <details class="path-detail robotics"><summary><span>PATH B</span><strong>ROBOTICS — QUESTION TYPES</strong></summary><div class="question-grid"><span>What information enters the system?</span><span>Which port controls this part?</span><span>Where does the system decide what to do?</span><span>If the sensor crossed your threshold, what might happen?</span></div></details>
      <details class="path-detail design"><summary><span>PATH C</span><strong>3D DESIGN — QUESTION TYPES</strong></summary><div class="question-grid"><span>Why did you choose this dimension?</span><span>What did Group do here?</span><span>How does this feature help the product work?</span><span>If this dimension became smaller, what could happen?</span></div></details>
    </div>

    <div class="cert-evidence">
      <span><b>WORKS</b>My creation does its main job.</span>
      <span><b>UNDERSTANDS</b>I can explain an important technical part.</span>
      <span><b>IMPROVES</b>I made and tested a purposeful change.</span>
      <span><b>TRANSFERS</b>I can predict what happens when something changes.</span>
    </div>

    <div class="outcome-grid">
      <article class="certified"><strong>LEVEL 1 CREATOR CERTIFIED</strong><p>You planned, built, tested, troubleshot, improved and explained your own creation.</p><span>CREATOR FOUNDATIONS COMPLETE</span></article>
      <article class="retry"><strong>RETRY ONE SKILL</strong><p>You are close. One part needs another try.</p><small>Mr. John will give you one specific thing to fix or demonstrate. <b>You do not restart Mission 8.</b></small></article>
      <article class="support"><strong>SUPPORT ROUTE</strong><p>You need a little more support before certification.</p><small>Work with Mr. John on the next small step. Continue from your current project.</small></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="stage passport">
    <div class="stage-head"><span class="stage-number">✓</span><div><p class="stage-kicker">FINAL LEVEL 1 PASSPORT</p><h2 class="stage-title">Level 1 Creator Passport</h2></div></div>
    <div class="check-list"><span>☐ I can choose tools that fit what I want to create.</span><span>☐ I can build a working program, system or design.</span><span>☐ I can test whether my creation actually works.</span><span>☐ I can troubleshoot problems one step at a time.</span><span>☐ I can improve my work based on evidence.</span><span>☐ I can explain important technical decisions.</span><span>☐ I can work independently while getting or giving appropriate help.</span><span>☐ I can use classroom technology and equipment responsibly.</span></div>
    <div class="completion-stamp"><span>LEVEL 1</span><strong>CREATOR FOUNDATIONS</strong><b>COMPLETE</b><small>CREATOR CERTIFIED</small></div>
    <p class="completion-message"><b>You finished Creator Foundations.</b> You started Level 1 by following guided steps. By Mission 8, you were planning, testing, troubleshooting, improving and explaining your own creation. <b>That growth is what Level 1 was about.</b></p>
    <p class="success"><b>Keep creating.</b></p>
  </section>

  <section class="stage showcase">
    <div class="stage-head"><span class="stage-number">★</span><div><p class="stage-kicker">OPTIONAL — AFTER CERTIFICATION</p><h2 class="stage-title">Share What You Made</h2></div></div>
    <p class="intro">Certified? If you have time, let someone else see what you created. <b>You are already certified. This part is just for sharing.</b></p>
    <div class="showcase-grid"><article><strong>TRY IT</strong><p>Let another student use your program or game.</p></article><article><strong>DEMO IT</strong><p>Show your robotic system to one or two classmates.</p></article><article><strong>DISPLAY IT</strong><p>Leave your CAD model open in a clear viewing angle.</p></article><article><strong>GALLERY</strong><p>Visit other completed creations around the room.</p></article></div>
  </section>

  <section class="stage reset">
    <div class="stage-head"><span class="stage-number">↺</span><div><p class="stage-kicker">BEFORE YOU LEAVE</p><h2 class="stage-title">Save, Reset & Return</h2></div></div>
    <div class="cleanup-grid">
      <article><strong>EVERYONE</strong><span>☐ Save the final version.</span><span>☐ Use a clear file name.</span><span>☐ Close unnecessary tabs.</span><span>☐ Update your Level 1 progress if Mr. John asks.</span><span>☐ Leave your workspace ready for the next person.</span></article>
      <article><strong>ROBOTICS</strong><span>☐ Power off.</span><span>☐ Disconnect carefully.</span><span>☐ Return all parts to the correct station.</span><span>☐ Report missing or damaged equipment.</span><span>☐ Release the station for another student.</span></article>
      <article><strong>3D DESIGN</strong><span>☐ Save the final digital model.</span><span>☐ Do not submit another print unless instructed.</span><span>☐ Printer availability does not affect certification.</span></article>
      <article><strong>CODING</strong><span>☐ Save the final program if required.</span><span>☐ Disconnect physical hardware properly.</span></article>
    </div>
  </section>
</FutureTechMissionFrame>

<style is:global>
.mission-body{grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr)}
.final-brief{display:grid;gap:.38rem;margin:0 0 .8rem;padding:1rem;border-radius:16px;background:linear-gradient(135deg,#111827,#312e81);color:#fff;border:1px solid #4338ca}.final-brief>span{color:#67e8f9;font-size:.7rem;font-weight:950;letter-spacing:.1em}.final-brief p{margin:0;color:#e5e7eb;line-height:1.5}.final-brief strong{color:#c4b5fd;font-size:.9rem}
.cert-flow{display:flex;justify-content:center;gap:.4rem;align-items:center;flex-wrap:wrap;padding:.62rem;border-radius:12px;background:#f5f3ff;border:1px solid #ddd6fe}.cert-flow span{padding:.32rem .46rem;border-radius:999px;background:#fff;color:#5b21b6;font-size:.68rem;font-weight:900}.cert-flow b{color:#7c3aed}.flow-note{text-align:center;margin:.35rem 0 .8rem;color:#667085;font-size:.84rem;font-weight:700}
